   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the implementation of the Regional Water Scarcity Initiative (WSI) in the Near East and North Africa (NENA) Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Overall objective: the overall objective of the programme is to contribute to the achievement of the water-related targets of the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development, with particular emphasis on &quot;No Poverty&quot; (SDG 1), &quot;Zero Hunger&quot; (SDG 2), &quot;Clean water and Sanitation&quot; (SDG 6), &quot;Affordable and Clean Energy&quot; (SDG 7), &quot;Climate Action&quot; (SDG 13), &quot;Life on Land&quot; (SDG 15), and &quot;Partnership for Goals&quot; (SDG 17).

Specific objective: the specific objective of the programme is to support water users and managers in the NENA countries in strengthening the planning and management of water resources in a sustainable manner to achieve water, food, and energy security under growing water scarcity and rapidly changing climate.</narrative>
  </description>
